 "question": "For fiscal 2023, which company had the higher operating margin: Alphabet (fiscal year ended December 31, 2023) or Microsoft (fiscal year ended June 30, 2023)? By how many percentage points did the higher one exceed the other?",
 "status": "completed",
 "termination_reason": "answered",
 "final_answer": {
  "text": "Microsoft had the higher operating margin in fiscal 2023: about 41.8% (operating income $88,523M on revenue $211,915M, FY ended June 30, 2023). Alphabet's was about 27.4% ($84,293M on $307,394M, FY ended Dec 31, 2023). Microsoft's margin was higher by about 14.35 percentage points.",
